# TestJavaToCSharpFernflower: fernflower's main sources printed as C# by maddi-cst-print-csharp and judged by Roslyn
# (tools/csharp-check, Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp 5.0.0 on .NET 10; see JavaToCSharpRatchet's javadoc). Lower is
# better for printerCrashes, syntaxErrors and unmappedJdkUses, higher for syntaxCleanFiles and compilingFiles;
# `types` must not move. Write a better value here in the commit that earns it.
#
# 2026-10-10, first record: the first slice of the printer, no BCL mapping. 0 printer crashes, 0 syntax errors; 22 of
# 199 files compile (interfaces and stubs); 5,290 errors (not ratcheted), 3,216 of them JDK types C# does not know.
# 2026-10-10, C#'s scoping of locals (a name an enclosing block declares later, two pattern variables of one name in
# a block: renamed) and jagged-array initializers (new T[] { } for a nested one): 23 files compile; 4,947 errors.
# 2026-10-10, the JDK -> BCL mapping (CSharpBcl): collections as List/Dictionary/HashSet, streams as LINQ, functional
# interfaces as delegates, exceptions, String/StringBuilder/boxed members, and the compatibility library
# Maddi.JavaCompat (JavaCompat.cs, compiled with the translation) where Java's behaviour differs: 105 files compile;
# unmapped JDK uses 6,922 -> 232; errors 4,947 -> 807.
# 2026-10-10, Java's Map and Set as IDictionary/ISet, LinkedHashMap as OrderedDictionary; unboxing casts and null as
# default for a type parameter where C# needs them; Java's iterators and java.io.File in the compatibility library;
# enums printed as classes get Name/Ordinal/Values/ValueOf; interface constants qualified; an exception's cause
# constructor: 124 files compile; unmapped JDK uses 232 -> 120; errors 807 -> 476.
# 2026-10-10, a static nested type of a generic type hoisted into the namespace; a boxed key or element passed to a
# collection or a type parameter unboxed; a raw array creation typed as declared: 132 files compile; errors 476 -> 310.
# 2026-10-10, a static member outside C#'s lookup scope (a static import, an interface's constant) qualified with its
# type; no using directive for an unmapped JDK package: 133 files compile; errors 310 -> 259.
# 2026-10-10, a local class that captures nothing lifted into its enclosing type: 134 files compile; errors 259 -> 236.
# 2026-10-10, a lambda or method reference of a translated functional interface wrapped in the interface's adapter
# class (new IExprentIterator.Lambda(e => ...)): 137 files compile; errors 236 -> 218.
# 2026-10-10, an anonymous class of a translated functional interface as a lambda in its adapter; an unbound method
# reference's lambda typed; Comparator.comparing with its compared type: 139 files compile; errors 218 -> 204.
# 2026-10-10, constructor rules (new FileOutputStream(f) -> new FileStream(..., FileMode.Create)); file and buffered
# streams, readers and writers; Pattern as Regex with the compatibility library's JavaMatcher; Instant, ThreadLocal,
# OptionalInt, Character.getType: 144 files compile; unmapped JDK uses 120 -> 74; errors 204 -> 156.
# 2026-10-10, unboxing in a conditional's branches, a compound assignment and an arithmetic operand, not of a lambda's
# parameter; a char switch's int labels as chars: 151 files compile; errors 156 -> 135.
# 2026-10-10, whole-program facts (CSharpProgram): a functional interface nothing implements is a delegate
# (DirectGraph.ExprentIterator, FastExtendedPostdominanceHelper.IReachabilityAction); the numbers do not move.
# 2026-10-10, closed world: a class nothing extends sealed, a method nothing overrides not virtual (237 of 267
# classes sealed, 38 virtual methods left); the numbers do not move.
# 2026-10-10, anonymous classes hoisted into private nested classes (captures as constructor arguments, the
# enclosing instance as outer): 152 files compile; errors 135 -> 140, the hoisted bodies being printed now (wildcard
# covariance, Map.Entry implementations, ClassLoader).
# 2026-10-10, List/Collection/Set/Iterable of ? extends T as C#'s covariant IReadOnlyList/IReadOnlyCollection/
# IEnumerable of T (wildcard losses 31 -> 16): 154 files compile; errors 140 -> 134.
# 2026-10-10, new EnumMap<>(K.class) as new SortedDictionary<K, V>(); == between a value type and an Object as
# object.Equals: 155 files compile; errors 134 -> 129.
# 2026-10-10, java.util.zip and java.util.jar as the compatibility library's classes over System.IO.Compression,
# Enumeration as JavaEnumeration: 160 files compile; unmapped JDK uses 74 -> 36; errors 129 -> 102.
# 2026-10-10, clone as a method of its own (super.clone() is MemberwiseClone); a for-each that assigns its variable
# works on a copy; a private type in a non-private signature is internal; Queue.poll and kin; removeIf on a set or a
# map's entries; AbstractMap.SimpleEntry as the compatibility library's JavaEntry; marker interfaces dropped: 168
# files compile; unmapped JDK uses 36 -> 32; errors 102 -> 89.
# 2026-10-10, a class extending ArrayList extends the compatibility library's JavaArrayList (LIST_SUBCLASS); Java's
# sorts stable, Collections.reverse in place: 170 files compile; errors 89 -> 78.
# 2026-10-10, a nested type as visible as the members whose signatures name it, and its enclosing types with it:
# 171 files compile; errors 78 -> 72.
# 2026-10-10, Iterator as the compatibility library's interface IJavaIterator<T>; a class implementing Iterable gets
# GetEnumerator; a conditional's null branch for a type parameter is default; Map.Entry.comparingByKey/Value with
# both type arguments ({R0.1} in templates): 176 files compile; errors 72 -> 60.
# 2026-10-10, interface implementations: a narrower return type implements the interface's method explicitly, a
# default method implements an inherited interface's method explicitly, an abstract class redeclares the interface
# methods it leaves (and its subclasses override them), clashing hoisted nested types are prefixed: 177 files
# compile; errors 60 -> 55.
